Fortunately for the two,
Dr. Jack Shephard

30:43.176 --> 30:46.804
was near the scene, pulled the victims
from the burning wreckage,

30:46.888 --> 30:50.058
and treated them at the scene
until paramedics arrived.

30:50.141 --> 30:53.478
The victims were later transported
to St. Sebastian hospital.

30:53.561 --> 30:56.647
Further details of their condition
have not been released.

31:06.407 --> 31:09.494
I'm going back. — what?

31:09.577 --> 31:13.331
I'm going back to the beach.
— no way. We keep moving.

31:13.414 --> 31:15.083
I ain't asking permission.

31:22.173 --> 31:23.883
Look, you got a job to do here.

31:23.966 --> 31:26.844
I ain't gonna stand
in your way of you doing it.

31:26.928 --> 31:28.513
But you sure don't need me.

31:28.596 --> 31:31.766
What do you think you're gonna get done,
alone and unarmed?

31:31.849 --> 31:34.185
He won't be alone. I'll go with him.
— no.

31:38.356 --> 31:40.775
Twenty minutes ago,
you weren't even going,

31:40.858 --> 31:42.527
and now you're telling Jack...

31:42.610 --> 31:44.529
I didn't want to go with you.

31:47.156 --> 31:49.617
Sawyer, it's a suicide mission
without guns.

31:49.700 --> 31:52.203
I know where there are some guns.

31:52.286 --> 31:54.831
There's a hidden cache
a couple miles from here.

31:54.914 --> 31:57.875
I can take us back
to the beach on a route past it.

31:57.959 --> 32:00.169
Juliet, you don't have to do that.

32:00.711 --> 32:03.131
Yeah, Jack, I kinda do.

32:19.063 --> 32:22.483
Don't do anything stupid.
— I won't if you won't.

32:32.869 --> 32:34.537
Don't wait up.

32:47.925 --> 32:52.555
[Charlie singing]

32:53.264 --> 32:54.891
I told you to shut up!

32:54.974 --> 32:57.435
You know when you get a tune
stuck in your head?

32:57.518 --> 32:59.478
This song just started coming to me.

33:00.855 --> 33:03.774
I just need to find the bridge.
— get the spear gun.

33:03.900 --> 33:05.943
What? Why?
— because I want it to hurt.

33:06.027 --> 33:09.405
No. Ben said we have to...
— you don't wanna get it? I will.

33:09.947 --> 33:11.227
Ix:,< (n f2~ (aw 73. Ll 5 q5 q5

33:12.283 --> 33:15.203
on on I'll shut up! I'll shut up!
I'll shut up!

33:19.916 --> 33:21.209
Il \\I/ u; ;\

33:23.628 --> 33:26.130
I thought you two
were on assignment in Canada.

33:30.384 --> 33:32.678
He made us promise not to tell anyone.

33:33.221 --> 33:35.806
Hello again.
— where is the other one?

33:36.265 --> 33:39.060
What?
— this idiot swam down from a boat.

33:39.143 --> 33:43.064
I was just shooting at his friend.
He dove down here.

33:43.147 --> 33:45.358
He's alone.
— are you sure about that?

33:46.817 --> 33:49.195
Here's a better question
to ask, cyclops.

33:49.278 --> 33:51.739
Why did your little friend Ben
tell you people

33:51.822 --> 33:54.575
that this entire station was flooded
when it isn't?

33:54.659 --> 33:58.913
Or why these two have been jamming
transmissions off the island?

34:02.416 --> 34:04.085
'A 73.73. (Fix w
(5'q5q5 m ///r x w. J,

34:04.168 --> 34:05.836
that's Ben. — I'll get it.

34:05.920 --> 34:08.422
[Beeping continues]

34:12.343 --> 34:15.721
You have to understand.
Everything I did, I did for the island.

34:15.805 --> 34:19.100
The island told you it was necessary
to jam your own people?

34:19.183 --> 34:22.561
Yes, it did.
You've always been a loyalist, mikhail.

34:22.645 --> 34:27.066
Now I'm asking you to trust me,
to trust Jacob, who told me to do this.

34:27.149 --> 34:29.735
Why would Jacob
ask you to lie to your own people?

34:31.904 --> 34:35.658
By forces stronger than anything
it's had to deal with in many years.

34:35.741 --> 34:39.287
And we are meant to protect it,
mikhail, by any means necessary.

34:39.370 --> 34:42.957
The jamming was for everyone's security.

34:48.254 --> 34:50.464
So why not trust me?

34:52.967 --> 34:56.178
I should have told you and I apologize.

34:58.723 --> 35:00.975
Mikhail? Are you still there?

35:09.650 --> 35:12.320
I need you to help me.

35:13.404 --> 35:17.199
I need you to help me clean up
this mess that I've made.

35:19.076 --> 35:21.412
I need you to kill Charlie.

35:22.371 --> 35:26.417
Make sure that the jamming mechanism
continues to function at all costs.

35:26.542 --> 35:30.046
We can't risk Greta and Bonnie
telling the others what we've done.

35:30.129 --> 35:32.882
So you'll have
to take care of them too.

35:37.053 --> 35:40.097
How do I know you didn't say
the same thing to them about me?

35:40.181 --> 35:44.935
Because if I had, mikhail,
you'd already be dead.

36:08.417 --> 36:09.794
You ok?

36:11.587 --> 36:14.298
Yeah. I just got a rock in my shoe.

36:24.558 --> 36:25.976
He didn't mean it, you know.

36:28.145 --> 36:30.189
What? — Sawyer.

36:31.273 --> 36:34.819
When he said that he didn't want
you to come go him, he didn't mean it.

36:34.902 --> 36:37.446
If he didn't mean it, why'd he say it?

36:38.030 --> 36:40.449
He was trying to protect you.

36:43.411 --> 36:45.788
That's why I asked you
not to come back for me.

36:51.335 --> 36:55.840
Hey. Why are you sticking up for Sawyer?

36:55.923 --> 36:57.716
He'd never do it for you.

37:04.390 --> 37:06.267
Because I love you.

37:28.372 --> 37:31.417
[Sawyer] When you pulled us out
of those polar bear cages

37:31.500 --> 37:33.461
and put us on the chain gang,

37:33.544 --> 37:36.213
what did you have us
breaking all those rocks for?

37:36.297 --> 37:39.383
We were building a runway.
— a runway? For what?

37:43.637 --> 37:46.974
I don't know what for.
Do you think they told me everything?

37:47.057 --> 37:49.059
Yeah, yeah. Whatever you say.

37:50.978 --> 37:54.273
So you screwing Jack yet?
— no. Are you?

37:55.232 --> 37:57.109
[Snickers]

37:57.193 --> 38:00.237
How far away are these guns?
— there aren't any guns.

38:01.822 --> 38:03.949
What? — I lied.

38:04.033 --> 38:07.369
You lied?
— It was the only way he'd let us go.

38:14.084 --> 38:15.794
So why are you going back?

38:18.756 --> 38:21.342
Why are you going back, James?

38:25.262 --> 38:27.264
Hey, guys! Wait up!

38:29.225 --> 38:32.019
What the hell do you want?
— I'm coming with you guys.

38:32.102 --> 38:34.939
Uh—uh. No way, not a chance.

38:35.022 --> 38:38.734
Come on, I can help!
They're my friends too, man.

38:39.401 --> 38:41.445
Charlie wouldn't let me go with him.

38:41.529 --> 38:45.115
And Jack's too busy leading
to even talk to me.

38:46.200 --> 38:48.118
I just wanna help. Please?

38:50.704 --> 38:54.875
For god sakes, Hugo, look at you.
You're just gonna get in the way.

38:56.377 --> 38:58.712
You wanna get us killed?

39:02.007 --> 39:03.467
Come on.

39:18.107 --> 39:22.861
If we head north, we should get to them
before they reach the tower.

39:23.404 --> 39:24.905
Why did you let me come?

39:24.989 --> 39:28.450
I let you come because
I'm delivering you to your new family.

39:29.952 --> 39:33.247
I let you come
because you betrayed me, Alex.

39:33.330 --> 39:35.207
You locked Karl in a cage.

39:35.291 --> 39:37.835
You put him in a room
and tried to brainwash him.

39:38.836 --> 39:42.089
I didn't want him to get you pregnant.

39:42.172 --> 39:44.008
I suppose I overreacted.

39:46.343 --> 39:48.470
We'd better get going. — Ben...

39:49.513 --> 39:53.934
Why do you have to stop them?
Why won't you just let them leave?

39:56.854 --> 39:59.857
Because I can't, Alex.

40:44.234 --> 40:46.862
[Breathing heavy]

41:37.913 --> 41:40.040
[Murmuring sound]

41:40.124 --> 41:41.959
[Boy] Don't, John.

41:48.966 --> 41:50.175
Put the gun down.

41:55.639 --> 41:57.808
Now, get up, John.

42:00.477 --> 42:05.274
He shot me, and I can't move my legs.

42:05.357 --> 42:09.069
You can move your legs.
Now, get out of the ditch, John.

42:10.446 --> 42:11.905
Why?

42:11.989 --> 42:14.908
Because you have work to do.
